  "key_findings": [
    "Prior Alpha158 LightGBM has materially stronger 9M all-market Rank IC/ICIR than current QuantMind 28-feature LightGBM.",
    "Daily same-session open-to-close round trips are not decision-grade unless T+0 eligibility is verified; both 22-stock Top-5 intraday variants lose after 20 bps per side.",
    "When converted to next-open-to-next-open holding with turnover-aware costs, QuantMind performs best at 3-session rebalance (+39.46%) but trails equal-weight buy-and-hold of the same 22 names (+43.46%).",
    "Prior model with TopK dropout-like n_drop=1 produces +52.37% in the simplified next-open simulator and beats the 22-name buy-and-hold benchmark, but requires exact Qlib engine validation before any trading conclusion."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The 22-stock universe was selected using later-2026 screening, so January-August replay has universe-selection look-ahead and is diagnostic, not strict PIT.",
    "Simplified open-to-open strategy sweep is not the exact QuantMind/Qlib order engine; it models next-open execution, equal weights, turnover costs and missing opens conservatively.",
    "No slippage, taxes, market impact, broker restrictions or exchange-certified T+0/T+1 eligibility are included.",
    "Current QuantMind feature adapter uses 48 requested features with IC/ICIR selection; it is not the full QuantDB 169+/429-factor production dataset."
  ]
